Fillets: an OnSame end whose face at the end continues the opposite face
tangentially, the contact a closed curve that comes round to that face's
surface again (mitcad#235).

The case: a recess's rim on a part's bottom rounded, the recess crossed by
a rib whose bottom is the part's bottom, the rib's edges with the bottom
rounded. Each half of the rim's rounding ends at the rib; the face at the
end is the rib's rounding, tangent to the bottom (the opposite face) along
the prolonged edge. IntersUpdateOnSame took the point where the contact
on the bottom, a circle round the recess's axis, meets the rounding's
surface: the contact only touches that surface (it lies on the bottom,
which the surface touches along the edge), at both ends of the half, and
the intersection gave the far end's touch, a diameter away. The cap was
then sought between the two ends ("echec calcul intersection") or the
point was the other corner's.

- IntersUpdateOnSame: where the surfaces are tangent along the prolonged
  edge (ChFi3d::IsTangentFaces with the face at the end taken either way:
  the orientation the corner passes it with is not the face's in the
  solid), both the intersection and the contact's crossing with the
  prolonged edge (until now sought only when the intersection found
  nothing) are computed, and the one nearer the corner's vertex is taken.
  Elsewhere the intersection alone, as before.

Before, the rounding failed at both ends. Test: a disc's recess crossed by
a rib, its rim rounded (geometry test_fillet_results).

